**Status (2026-08-30, night — D13 shipped):** deterministic entity
resolution. `EntityId::from_external(org, table_uuid, logical_pk)` — a
domain-separated, length-prefixed digest over the EXTERNAL coordinates,
deliberately independent of source, producer, name, and mapping version
(the row is the same row) — and ingest stamps it onto every
snapshot-provenance memory beside the name-extracted entities. The same
external row arriving through two producers now converges on one join
point with zero fuzzy matching, and `find_by_entity` returns both
producers' memories (pinned by a cross-producer test). The
name-based space and the external space cannot collide. The fuzzy/
probabilistic half stays D17, unstarted, as designed.

**Status (2026-08-30, night — D18 shipped):** the git-history adapter
(`crates/exocortex-adapter-git`) — the cheapest real adapter and the
strongest zero-friction demo — runs against any local checkout:
`fix:`-prefixed commits map to `Fix`, everything else to `Command`, each
changed path gets an identity-stable `FileContext` memory, and the one
relationship git states factually (`Modifies`) becomes the edges; commit
content carries author/date/paths so server-side entity extraction
converges File/Person entities as it does for wrapups. ExternalKey
identity (repo-scoped table uuid, sha/path logical pks) makes re-runs
idempotent; the adapter declares a D21 projection (window bound enforced
pre-wire); a fixture git repo drives the hermetic integration suite.
PR/issue joins stay with D19 (no text guessing), per the recorded
boundary.

**Status (2026-08-30, later — Wave 2 opened, D21 steps a+d shipped):**
The adapter contract's unblocking pair landed. `RegisterSource` gained a
`ProjectionDescriptor` (selector, field mapping, declared source schema,
bounds, mapping version) — REQUIRED for table-shaped flavors; the SDK
gained `AdapterConfig.projection` with window/run bound enforcement that
stops the window before any wire traffic, names the bound, and leaves
the cursor untouched, plus rewind detection
(`SdkError::SourceRewound`). The server stores the projection with a
canonical schema hash, refuses unmapped/undeclared registrations,
requires a `mapping_version` bump for any change, and evaluates the D4
schema-evolution verdict table at re-registration: unmapped additions
are accepted with exactly one audit row; removal/retype/rename fail
closed. Submit enforces `PROJECTION_BOUND_EXCEEDED`, `SCHEMA_DRIFT`
(two new wire reject codes with corrections + playbook rows), and
`SOURCE_REWOUND` (bounded in-memory snapshot history; durability is
D20's open question 3). Acceptance rows ac1/ac4 verified, ac2/ac3/ac5
tracked to steps b/c/e. Steps b (PreflightBatch), c (rulebook-as-data
manifest), and e (`xtask adapter-contract` gate) remain — D18/D13 next.

**Status (2026-08-30, Wave 1 complete):** PX2 shipped —
pack-registered Actions and Functions end to end. The `pack!` macro grew
`actions!` / `functions!` / `guidance!` sections (plain `macro_rules!`,
per the PX2-S1 decision); signatures join the compatibility fingerprint
while bodies stay out of `PackDef` entirely, so a body patch moves
neither level. The mortgage pack declares `AttachRuleFinding` (typed
action, Project ceiling) and `IsCategoricallyEligible` (scheme function);
the ops framework runs them — caller-ceiling check, one-implementation
preflight, provenance stamping, and a new audited batch commit seam
(`upsert_batch_audited`, rows + audit row in one storage operation).
Pack verbs join the ONE operation registry (`OperationEntry.pack`,
merged `entries()`), so MCP/OpenAPI/parity pick them up for free; the
client gained `--dump-tools` (typed schemas) and `--dump-fingerprint`;
`gen-playbook` renders `guidance!` tables with computed-only kinds
subtracted; and the generated Function-SLO bench harness
(`ops/benches/pack_functions.rs`) enumerates the `functions!` registry
against declared budgets. Acceptance rows px1-px8. The intended
fingerprint move is recorded (compatibility now `2c3ec388…5c23`, build
`18dbf33b…49f5` over the composed pack set; goldens updated in the same
change). **Wave 2 (D21/D18/D19/D13/D1/PX4) is next.**

