ime_paths` + `resolve_paths_names_missing_runtime_files`; the CI-exact RELATIVE-layout invocation of `scripts/test-standalone-live.sh` failed pre-fix with the dlopen message captured and passes post-fix — the strongest fail-without-fix). **Secondary floors (proven binary facts; both runners would still fail after the path fix):** the darwin-arm64 `falkordb.so` declares `minos 15.0` (`otool LC_BUILD_VERSION`) so macos-14 can never load it -> arm64 release leg moved to `macos-15`; the linux-x64 `redis-server` references `GLIBC_2.38` symbols while ubuntu-22.04 ships 2.35 -> the linux leg keeps its ubuntu-22.04 BUILDER (shipped binaries keep their glibc 2.35 floor) and validates the packaged artifact inside the digest-pinned `falkordb/falkordb` trixie userland (glibc 2.41; libgomp/libssl3/libcrypto3/libstdc++6 verified present by executing the pinned image). **Diagnosability (the row's original fix requirement):** `wait_ping`'s exit path now names exit status (code or signal) plus the bounded 2 KiB tail of the store's own log with BOTH stdout and stderr joined to the sink — redis logs its startup output to STDOUT, which is exactly why the first stderr-only capture came back empty on run 33590545074 (`startup_failure_names_the_cause`, proved fails-by-stash). The cross-invocation-teardown suspicion is disproven: the ubuntu leg of run 33543324895 died on the FIRST invocation with no prior wrapper run, and the restart-durability leg (which exercises teardown) passes locally end to end. Floors recorded at every user surface (RUNTIME-MANIFEST.txt, installer refusal, README-install.txt, README, PUBLISHING.md; milestone deviation 21; the missing numbered deviation-20 entry the plan already cited was also written). Run 33590545074 (the re-tag with only the floors+path story) then exposed TWO further stacked defects, both fixed in the same closure: (a) the darwin-arm64 module dlopens Homebrew libomp and openssl@3 at absolute /opt/homebrew paths — absent on stock machines (runners