| D7 | **3** | Contradiction-resolution op (§23 #13) | §23 #13, round-2 H14 | **Done** — `resolve_contradiction` in the ONE registry (MCP/HTTP parity-covered): a human decision over an open `Contradicts` edge (from|to|neither + mandatory note) closes the edge (new version, `valid_until`, so it stops firing the detector), supersedes the loser to the exact stale-belief floor the commit path applies to `Replaces`/`Contradicts` targets (never deletes — reversible history), and writes the decision to the audit ledger in the SAME atomic commit (`upsert_batch_audited`). Refuses everything else by name: non-Contradicts edges, already-resolved edges, invisible endpoints (IN2 pattern), empty notes. `parity.rs::resolve_contradiction_supersedes_closes_and_audits`; §23 criterion 13 verified |
