| D13 | **2** | **Deterministic entity resolution** — resolve the same real-world entity across producers by shared external identity (`ExternalKey`, typed entities as convergent join points), not by fuzzy matching. Explicitly NOT the ML half: no corpus, no labelled set, no model. Without this the graph is a collection of documents rather than a model of a world, which is the core ontology claim. Fuzzy/probabilistic ER is a separate later item, and `NearDuplicateApplicant` stays a Dreams-computed proposal in the meantime | palantir-expansion PRD §5; core PRD §24 | **Done** — kernel `EntityId::from_external` (domain-separated from the name space, length-prefixed so table/pk boundaries cannot blur, org-scoped; `ids.rs::external_entity_identity_is_deterministic_and_domain_separated`); ingest `attach_entities` stamps the external join point on every snapshot-provenance memory over the canonical hex table rendering (B8); cross-producer convergence + retrieval pinned in `schema_evolution.rs::external_identity_joins_across_producers`; `mapping_version` deliberately does not fork the join (the row is the same row) |
